# Store this vendored tree verbatim.
#
# Git's line-ending normalisation rewrote LICENSE and README.md on the way in,
# so the committed blobs differed from the crates.io tarball while the working
# tree matched it. That is harmless in itself and corrosive to the thing this
# fork's removal condition rests on: "still present with no local modifications"
# has to be a question you can *answer*, and it stops being one as soon as some
# files differ for reasons that are not modifications.
#
# `-text` keeps every byte, so `cmp` against a fresh tarball is a straight
# yes/no. See VENDORED.md.
* -text
